---
description: Spec-driven development expectations
alwaysApply: true
---

- Meaningful behavior changes start by updating `specs/` and, when the behavior is governed, `.specify/memory/constitution.md`.
- Spec Kit skills live in `.cursor/skills` and are owned by the Spec Kit CLI. Do not hand-edit those skill files.
- Project rules in `.cursor/rules` are separate from Spec Kit skills.
- Trivial copy or type fixes do not need a new specification.
- After implementation, update the spec if the code intentionally changed the contract.
